,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":181.120803982,"data":"RESULT_JSON::{\"example_id\": \"DAPT01EVAL-002\", \"arm\": \"base_norag\", \"question\": \"According to Stevenson's Notes on Modern Jainism, what is Karma, and how does it affect a person's lives?\", \"answer\": \"According to Stevenson's Notes on Modern Jainism, Karma is a fundamental concept in Jainism that refers to the moral law of cause and effect. It is believed that every action, thought, and word generates karma, which can either bind or liberate a person. Positive actions lead to good karma, while negative actions result in bad karma. This accumulated karma influences a person's current and future lives, determining their experiences and circumstances. The ultimate goal in Jainism is to achieve liberation (moksha) by purifying oneself of all karma.\", \"prompt_style\": \"chat_template\", \"system_prompt\": \"You are a careful assistant for Jain studies. Answer the user's question concisely (in 1-3 sentences). If you are unsure or the information is not available, say so.\", \"decoding\": \"greedy\", \"max_new_tokens\": 192, \"new_tokens\": 110, \"decode_seconds\": 11.393, \"seed\": 42, \"rag\": false, \"input_prompt_sha256\": \"171ca062f3a8c052512952ee89bb2d66111396cfef7560e9eeeb378df2d4c0c9\"}\n"}
