,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1076.530399503,"data":"RESULT_JSON::{\"example_id\": \"DAPT01EVAL-003\", \"arm\": \"dapt_norag\", \"question\": \"According to Stevenson, what are the two great divisions of Jain cosmic time, and how many periods does each contain?\", \"answer\": \"Stevenson identifies the two great divisions of Jain cosmic time as the Satya Kalpa (true era) and the Avasarpini Kalpa (descending era). The Satya Kalpa contains 24 periods, while the Avasarpini Kalpa contains 27 periods. These periods represent the cyclical nature of time in Jain cosmology, reflecting the continuous cycle of creation, destruction, and rebirth.\", \"prompt_style\": \"chat_template\", \"system_prompt\": \"You are a careful assistant for Jain studies. Answer the user's question concisely (in 1-3 sentences). If you are unsure or the information is not available, say so.\", \"decoding\": \"greedy\", \"max_new_tokens\": 192, \"new_tokens\": 87, \"decode_seconds\": 14.88, \"seed\": 42, \"rag\": false, \"input_prompt_sha256\": \"0a6c8cf1a2e27c4da15f759197ca7b1545dd9a9e8098f4f576fc2742d277b41a\"}\n"}
