,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1941.572031403,"data":"RESULT_JSON::{\"example_id\": \"DAPT01EVAL-039\", \"arm\": \"dapt_norag\", \"question\": \"How many Agams do the Digambara tradition accept?\", \"answer\": \"The Digambara tradition accepts 24 Agams. These Agams are considered to be the sacred scriptures of the Jain community, containing the teachings of the Tirthankars. The content of these Agams is believed to have been lost over time, leaving only the names and a few details. The Svetambara tradition, on the other hand, accepts 25 Agams, including the 24 Agams accepted by the Digambaras plus the Anga, which is considered a separate scripture. The Anga is believed to have been lost by the Digambaras, further highlighting the differences between the two traditions.\", \"prompt_style\": \"chat_template\", \"system_prompt\": \"You are a careful assistant for Jain studies. Answer the user's question concisely (in 1-3 sentences). If you are unsure or the information is not available, say so.\", \"decoding\": \"greedy\", \"max_new_tokens\": 192, \"new_tokens\": 132, \"decode_seconds\": 24.7, \"seed\": 42, \"rag\": false, \"input_prompt_sha256\": \"9ca1e87f118342d2e3bae1bb5de4501d7390fc00e0a5dd068fb4192a69ee7741\"}\n"}
