,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2138.724496057,"data":"RESULT_JSON::{\"example_id\": \"DAPT01EVAL-002\", \"arm\": \"dapt_rrf250\", \"question\": \"According to Stevenson's Notes on Modern Jainism, what is Karma, and how does it affect a person's lives?\", \"answer\": \"Karma, according to Stevenson, is a force that binds the soul to the material world, preventing its liberation. It is a consequence of actions, both physical and mental, that creates a cycle of birth and death. The nature, duration, quality, and quantity of karma determine the experiences of the soul in its current and future lives. The soul's actions in one life influence its circumstances in the next, creating a chain of cause and effect that spans multiple lifetimes. This understanding of karma emphasizes the importance of ethical conduct and spiritual practices for breaking free from the cycle of rebirth and achieving liberation.\", \"prompt_style\": \"chat_template\", \"system_prompt\": \"You are a careful assistant for Jain studies. Answer the user's question concisely (in 1-3 sentences). If you are unsure or the information is not available, say so.\", \"decoding\": \"greedy\", \"max_new_tokens\": 192, \"new_tokens\": 122, \"decode_seconds\": 23.309, \"seed\": 42, \"rag\": true, \"input_prompt_sha256\": \"acd224e5b71ec0336f1e2805be17d1fb129647da65323325c8b3a56768997a45\", \"evidence_context_sha256\": \"4cf5600019a25dface6887f0df0d018528c9603652a0eb95c692967f2b33f0a8\", \"n_evidence_items\": 5}\n"}
