,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2257.727401922,"data":"RESULT_JSON::{\"example_id\": \"DAPT01EVAL-006\", \"arm\": \"dapt_rrf250\", \"question\": \"According to Stevenson's account of the Sthanakavasi canon, how many Mulagrantha are there?\", \"answer\": \"According to Mrs. Sinclair Stevenson's account of the Sthanakavasi canon, there are four Mulagrantha. These are the Sutrakritanga, Dharma Sutra, Upadesha Sutra, and A'vasyaka Sutra. The Sthanakavasi accept only the first two as Mulagrantha, considering the A'vasyaka Sutra to be the last of all the scriptures. This differs from the Svetambara canon, which includes all four as Mulagrantha. The A'vasyaka Sutra is considered a scripture but not a Mulagrantha by the Sthanakavasi. This distinction highlights the differences in the Sthanakavasi and Svetambara traditions regarding the sacred texts.\", \"prompt_style\": \"chat_template\", \"system_prompt\": \"You are a careful assistant for Jain studies. Answer the user's question concisely (in 1-3 sentences). If you are unsure or the information is not available, say so.\", \"decoding\": \"greedy\", \"max_new_tokens\": 192, \"new_tokens\": 160, \"decode_seconds\": 29.556, \"seed\": 42, \"rag\": true, \"input_prompt_sha256\": \"89d07419d614167f335cd9242437ff76bb0c9b6a2e1a078c57eb63879882bd26\", \"evidence_context_sha256\": \"e3324c9670ecfac37d4e4395b113c6991b3252fc9c0a68ba7a14ff277f2d3d34\", \"n_evidence_items\": 5}\n"}
